    "title_en": "Identification of a nanosecond isomer of $^{164}$Tb",
    "abstract_en": "This letter reports on the identification of a new isomeric state of $^{164}$Tb ($Z=65$, $N=99$), which was measured with the DESPEC setup at the GSI Helmholtzzentrum für Schwerionenforschung GmbH following the first relativistic fragmentation of an $^{170}$Er primary beam. From the time distribution and coincidences of the emitted $\\gamma $ rays, the isomer is tentatively assigned to a state with spin-parity $(7^{-})$ at an excitation energy of $283.3(2)~\\textrm{keV}$ with a half-life of $159(11)~\\textrm{ns}$. The isomer is interpreted as the $\\pi 7/2^{-}[523]\\otimes \\nu 7/2^{+}[633]$ configuration from the Nilsson orbital systematics. These results represent the first report of $\\gamma $-ray spectroscopy of $^{164}$Tb, providing insight into the ground-state and low-lying level structure.",
